      {
        "id": 115083,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-17T14:01:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The rules do not say that Aim tokens go away, or even that they affect the next attack, those rules from playtesting appear to be gone.</p><p>You can save Aim tokens and use&nbsp;<strong>an aim token before an attack to gain its effect on one target you hit with that attack,&nbsp;</strong>so you could not spend 4 before an attack to use its effect on four different target.</p><p>You can save them up and use them on an overwhelm with a bunch of proletariats using hammer of the people on the next round.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Proletariat is almost unkillable with Defensive sacrifice and overwhelm (once you get a few copies out) you restock with overwhelm/duplicate, and if you don't need to do that you can overwhelm move/sprint, or overwhelm hammer the crap out of someone. &nbsp;When they turn to kill you you sacrifice your clones and restock them the next turn.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:47:09.306Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
