        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>The rules do not say that Aim tokens go away, or even that they affect the next attack, those rules from playtesting appear to be gone.</p><p>You can save Aim tokens and use&nbsp;<strong>an aim token before an attack to gain its effect on one target you hit with that attack,&nbsp;</strong>so you could not spend 4 before an attack to use its effect on four different target.</p><p>You can save them up and use them on an overwhelm with a bunch of proletariats using hammer of the people on the next round.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Proletariat is almost unkillable with Defensive sacrifice and overwhelm (once you get a few copies out) you restock with overwhelm/duplicate, and if you don&#39;t need to do that you can overwhelm move/sprint, or overwhelm hammer the crap out of someone. &nbsp;When they turn to kill you you sacrifice your clones and restock them the next turn.</p>",
