      {
        "id": 115084,
        "name": "Koga",
        "username": "Koga",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/{size}/2058_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-17T14:16:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The rules do not say that Aim tokens go away, or even that they affect the next attack, those rules from playtesting appear to be gone.</p>\n<p>You can save Aim tokens and use&nbsp;<strong>an aim token before an attack to gain its effect on one target you hit with that attack,&nbsp;</strong>so you could not spend 4 before an attack to use its effect on four different target.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Didn't realize you could only spend 1 Aim token per attack.</p>\n<p>As for keeping tokens, Page 4 under Turns in the Power Up phase:</p>\n<blockquote></blockquote>\n<p>Then, discard any Aim or Dodge tokens you have.</p>\n<p>You could still Overwhelm Dodge and use 1 each time you're atttacked.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
